WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.322 --> 00:00:03.155
[music]

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.810
[Instructor] Cool, so we've got a lot
of awesome functionality in our game now,

3
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.810
so you can see the Player jumping
because they're so excited,

4
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.180
and you see all of these Obstacles
moving through the Scene.

5
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.181
Now, the one thing that you notice
is that the Player is

6
00:00:17.611 --> 00:00:20.130
standing incredibly still.

7
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.300
Now, that's either
because of one of two reasons.

8
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.702
Either the Player is moving
so slow

9
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.070
that they're not actually moving
at all,

10
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.610
or the Player's moving so fast

11
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.160
that our eyes can't even perceive
how fast the Player's moving,

12
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.877
and so we can only see
it as standing still.

13
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:41.360
I'll leave
that up to your own interpretation.

14
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.660
So in order to actually make
the Player

15
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.820
look like they're moving 
in this Scene

16
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.170
that's constantly moving
back and forth,

17
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.890
we're going to need
to Play with

18
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.480
the Player's animation.

19
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.726
So what we're going to do is,
we're actually going

20
00:00:55.726 --> 00:00:58.783
to click on the Player, 
and then in their Inspector,

21
00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:01.170
you can see that there's actually
an Animator

22
00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.436
Component already applied to it,

23
00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.919
and it has a Controller
for a SimpleCharacter,

24
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.671
so what we can do is 
we can actually...

25
00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.430
double-click on that
SimpleCharacter box,

26
00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:16.340
and now you see that it actually
opens up

27
00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.850
a brand new window
in our Scene for Animators.

28
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.430
Now, if you want to see all
of the different windows

29
00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.570
that you could actually add to Unity,

30
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.870
you can actually see on the top-left
there's the "Window" button,

31
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.972
and then you can actually add a bunch
of other windows that you can use.

32
00:01:33.624 --> 00:01:36.989
One that you might've seen before;
actually, our console

33
00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:40.439
is where the game over message
is being sent.

34
00:01:41.019 --> 00:01:43.190
So you can add other windows
if you want to.

35
00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:45.280
So now, in our Animator window,

36
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.730
you can see that we have a strange view
of this button

37
00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.760
that says entry but not
really anything else.

38
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.450
You can actually move around in
this view, there's a lot more going on,

39
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.719
so we can press the Alt key,

40
00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.450
and hold it,
and then left-click,

41
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.814
and drag, and we can move around

42
00:02:01.524 --> 00:02:03.522
our little Animator window here,

43
00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:07.410
or we can use our mouse wheel,
and scroll in and out

44
00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.690
to zoom in and out, and if you click
on your mouse wheel,

45
00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.610
and hold,
and then you drag it around,

46
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.980
you can actually move
around that way.

47
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.071
So there's a lot of different
things happening

48
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.858
in our little
Animator window here.

49
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.820
Now first and foremost,
the Animator Controller

50
00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.180
is the way that we
actually control the states

51
00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.190
that the character is 
in at the current moment.

52
00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.605
So, in fact,
when we're pressing Play,

53
00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.900
our Animator Controller goes
straight to our "Idle" animation,

54
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.382
which is why it looks
like the Player is not moving at all.

55
00:02:38.512 --> 00:02:40.846
The Player's not moving,
surprise.

56
00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:43.710
They're not moving incredibly fast,
they're just not moving at all.

57
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.480
So our Animator Controller
actually controls

58
00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.150
all of the different states
that our character can be in,

59
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.980
so our character can be idle,

60
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.800
and then from idle,
these arrows actually mean

61
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.548
that they then can go into one 
of these different states.

62
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.310
So, it can go from idle
into a "Walk_Static" state,

63
00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.571
which means 
that they're not actually walking

64
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.066
in a direction, 
they're just walking in place.

65
00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.193
You can also run in place
with "Run_Static".

66
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.170
You can walk in a direction
using "Walk",

67
00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.080
or you can "Run" in a direction.

68
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.382
And so, if you started to move,
for example,

69
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.550
maybe it'll go to the Walk animation,
and then when you stop moving,

70
00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.630
it'll go back to your Idle animation
so you stand still.

71
00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.790
Now, a really cool thing is
you can actually see

72
00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.690
what these different animations
are like,

73
00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.720
so if we zoom in a little bit,

74
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.083
if we were to double-click on Idle,

75
00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:40.122
you can actually see that it pops
up a little animation preview,

76
00:03:40.862 --> 00:03:42.849
and we can actually press Play,

77
00:03:43.542 --> 00:03:45.880
and you can see that the Model

78
00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.417
isn't actually really doing
anything.

79
00:03:50.874 --> 00:03:54.481
You can see it's just kind of waving
its arms back and forth.

80
00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.117
If we choose, for example,
Walk_Static,

81
00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.505
double-click on that,
we have another animation,

82
00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.360
and so you can see
it actually looks

83
00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.500
like this character's
walking, which is cool.

84
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.449
If we double-click on run,
and we press Play,

85
00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.670
you can see that this one is
actually moving

86
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.920
through the Scene, compared
to if we go to...

87
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.510
run static,

88
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.540
this one runs in place,
so very helpful

89
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.473
to know the states
of all of these things.

90
00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.550
If we take a look at the arrows,

91
00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.580
you can actually see...

92
00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.399
all of the different conditions
that need to happen

93
00:04:35.399 --> 00:04:37.550
to actually make the character move,

94
00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:40.739
which we'll go into a little bit
on how we can edit those and see those.

95
00:04:41.089 --> 00:04:44.430
So you can see we have these conditions
for an actual speed, so say

96
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.663
the Player is not moving,
their speed is 0,

97
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.393
and then they start moving,
and it reaches a point where it's .25,

98
00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.516
then it will actually go
into this transition,

99
00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.430
and you can see this transition happen.

100
00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.487
So, they're stopped, 
and then they start moving,

101
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.803
and then it goes into walk static,

102
00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.440
and the Player is just moving.

103
00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.830
So, now what you're going to do is,

104
00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.989
you're going to left-click
on the Player in the Hierarchy,

105
00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:22.707
and then under the Inspector
in the Animator Component,

106
00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.883
where you see Controller,

107
00:05:24.883 --> 00:05:27.613
you're going to double-click
on SimpleCharacter.

108
00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:31.120
This will open 
up your Animator window

109
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.860
for your Player character,
and so now,

110
00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:37.810
you can go look around, and see
all of the different animation states,

111
00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.235
you can click into...

112
00:05:40.235 --> 00:05:42.670
the different states
by double-clicking on them,

113
00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:47.550
and then you can preview their different
animations like walking static

114
00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.690
or walking,

115
00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.679
and then you can take a look
at some of the different transitions,

116
00:05:56.679 --> 00:05:58.480
and see the different conditions

117
00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.479
that they need to follow 
to be able to move.

118
00:06:01.939 --> 00:06:03.939
Now it's your turn.

119
00:06:04.019 --> 00:06:06.852
[music]
